{"parentUuid":"a72dec82-5140-4f19-8b4d-11e265fa8e60","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"msg_011Cfg3iQ3jV18cYaGxMqJik","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5-5","stop_reason":"end_turn","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed ticket 6c8 and opened PR 167, but testing on studious showed that the app crashes on master whenever the chord is held.\n\nThe fix: a modifier change used to be dated by the event that triggered the reading. If the key was let go before that reading, the release got the earlier date, so a hold could be mistaken for a tap. Now each reading is dated by when the session last saw a modifier key move. All 607 tests pass, including one for the ticket's exact case: the release is now dated at 400 ms instead of 100.\n\nOn studious, the session dated each key 3 to 8 milliseconds before the event's own stamp, and holding Right Option started listening. But the app quit about 300 milliseconds later. The cause is on master, not this branch: a timer added in the last PR runs on the wrong thread and trips Swift's thread check, so holding the chord crashes the app every time. I filed it as urgent ticket c08, and it should be the next one up.\n\nThe next session starts the review passes on PR 167. Studious still has this branch's build installed."}],"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":335}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"99bc0d60-49e3-4e4d-92ff-f6ebe11f4f22","timestamp":"2026-10-03T21:54:14.624Z"}
